## Why This Is Asked

Tests expertise in geo-distributed, multi-tenant governance covering data residency requirements, cross-data center ordering guarantees, and traffic optimization under production load.

## Key Concepts

- Geo-distributed multi-tenant isolation and compliance
- Region-aware partitioning and leader election
- Cross-region replication throttling and causal ordering
- Canary rollout strategies and rollback mechanisms
- Compliance auditing and residency enforcement

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation sketch
class GeoPolicy {
  constructor(tenantRegionMap) { this.tenantRegionMap = tenantRegionMap; }

  getRegionsForTenant(tenantId) {
    return this.tenantRegionMap[tenantId] || ['default'];
  }

  enforceResidency(tenantId, targetRegion) {
    const allowedRegions = this.getRegionsForTenant(tenantId);
    return allowedRegions.includes(targetRegion);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle tenant region migrations with zero downtime?
- What monitoring metrics would you track for geo-replication health?
- How do you ensure consistency during network partitions?

Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical deletion workflows in multi-tenant KCNA, balancing legal rights, data minimization, and system integrity. It requires concrete mappings, key management, tombstone strategies, and test plans that prove irreversibility while keeping performance acceptable.

Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped data maps and identifiers
- Per-tenant key rotation and re-encryption
- Tombstones, garbage collection, and index scrubbing
- Auditing, proofs, and compliance testing
- Backups, restores, and consistency guarantees

Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation skeleton
function eraseTenantData(tenantId) {
  revokeAccess(tenantId);
  rotateKeys(tenantId);
  scrubIngest(tenantId);
  scrubEnrichment(tenantId);
  scrubAnalytics(tenantId);
  publishTombstones(tenantId);
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for complete deletion in a live cluster?
- How do backups interact with the deletion policy?
